From: nxrs contributors
Subject: [PATCH RFC] SelectionDAG: discard unused BR_CC simplifications before target combines

SimplifySetCC can return a speculative non-SETCC expression which BR_CC
cannot consume. That unused expression temporarily adds operand uses and
conceals one-use opportunities from target combines. Discard it with the
existing worklist-aware cleanup. Preserve live expressions and the existing
SETCC branch-folding path.

The preceding Xtensa bit-test regressions expose this independently of
instruction selection: the pre-fix selector fails nonzero single-bit tests
above bit zero, while zero tests already work. Its speculative SRL has no
users but keeps the AND at two uses until after the target combine. Run
the saved pre-fix compiler as a negative control, plus x86 branch and
overflow regressions.

This is an inactive generic RFC. Other targets and broader profitability
still require qualification; no application workaround is introduced.

diff --git a/llvm/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/DAGCombiner.cpp b/llvm/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/DAGCombiner.cpp
--- a/llvm/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/DAGCombiner.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/CodeGen/SelectionDAG/DAGCombiner.cpp
@@ -18827,5 +18827,9 @@
                        Simp.getOperand(0), Simp.getOperand(1),
                        N->getOperand(4));
 
+  // Discard unused speculative compares before target one-use checks.
+  if (Simp)
+    recursivelyDeleteUnusedNodes(Simp.getNode());
+
   return SDValue();
 }
